      "source": [
        "## 7. Define sentiment prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "For each review, add the log prior and known tokens' log likelihoods, normalize to log posterior probabilities, and choose the class with the higher value. Tokens absent from the training vocabulary are skipped. Predicting positive or negative labels for the test reviews is the required sentiment analysis on the test data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "4cbdfabe",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4cbdfabe"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import math\n",
        "\n",
        "def predict_review(tokens, priors, likelihoods, vocabulary):\n",
        "    scores = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "    for label in [0, 1]:\n",
        "        # Start with the class's log prior.\n",
        "        score = math.log(priors[label])\n",
        "\n",
        "        for word in tokens:\n",
        "            # Ignore unknown test tokens.\n",
        "            if word not in vocabulary:\n",
        "                continue\n",
        "\n",
        "            # Add each known token's log likelihood.\n",
        "            score += math.log(likelihoods[label][word])\n",
        "\n",
        "        scores[label] = score\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Normalize into log posterior probabilities.\n",
        "    max_score = max(scores.values())\n",
        "\n",
        "    log_normalizer = max_score + math.log(\n",
        "        sum(math.exp(score - max_score) for score in scores.values())\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    log_posteriors = {\n",
        "        label: score - log_normalizer\n",
        "        for label, score in scores.items()\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Choose the class with the highest log posterior.\n",
        "    prediction = max(log_posteriors, key=log_posteriors.get)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return prediction, log_posteriors"
      ]
    },
